WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:07.020
I want to know more about you someday, though.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.400
It's okay.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.270
I think I want you to know me, Mononobe.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.830
Mitsuki-san, do you insist that the 
guilt of having killed Miyako-san,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.000
and the need to atone for it, is yours alone?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.760
I'm confronting—

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.130
You don't even expect me to forgive you.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.100
Don't say things like that so lightly.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.480
I wish there was something I could do.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.050
It'd help if you'd cheer for us, then.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.230
I think that alone will bring our 
chances of success up really high.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.100
Okay.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.560
I'll cheer for everyone.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.150
We won't let the Dragon have you.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.370
Four, three, two, one.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.160
Fire!

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:28.070
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:40.490
<b>Mistilteinn Falls</b>

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.470
What?!

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.400
No!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.340
Yuu-san!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.220
All units, retreat immediately.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.550
Keep your altitude as low as possible.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.170
The operation team has returned.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.210
Increase speed.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.420
Leave the combat area.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.260
Tear-chan...

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.090
I'm sorry.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.150
I couldn't help you.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:08.620
We couldn't do anything but run.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.620
We lost.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:20.460
Mitsuki?

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.340
Mononobe Yuu.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.280
Thanks for your good work.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.440
It's thanks to you that 
everyone got back safely.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:41.150
No, it's thanks to Honoka. 
She broke my balance.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.240
Otherwise, we'd all be...

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.680
But there's no time to celebrate 
making it back alive.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.600
Now that our operation has failed,

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.560
NIFL won't stay quiet.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.250
I knew you'd be here.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.600
Nii-san.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.960
Don't let it get to you.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.310
The Basilisk had better detection 
capabilities than we expected.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.680
If you and Honoka-san hadn't been there,

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:23.780
we'd all have died.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:28.740
I couldn't protect anything, again.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.920
Blaming yourself for everything like that

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.710
is one of your bad habits.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.200
Keep that up,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.920
and you won't even last long 
enough to fight the Basilisk.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:46.340
You're still...

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.400
I'm not giving up.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.810
You made a promise with Lisa, too, didn't you?

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.380
Mitsuki's already decided 
how to confront her guilt.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:59.400
So I want you to think about 
how you'll forgive her.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.360
You're very partial toward 
your sister, aren't you?

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.360
Fine, then. I'll think of an 
impossibly difficult condition.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.220
Has Lisa said anything?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.330
No, nothing yet.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.370
I see.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:20.740
Listen, Mitsuki.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.880
I don't want you taking all 
the responsibility upon yourself,

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.840
or breaking your promise with Lisa.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:28.920
So don't give up.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:32.050
Nii-san...

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.020
We have to do what we can 
to the best of our abilities.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:46.210
Yes.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:48.980
<i>Altitude: 2,000.</i>

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.700
<i>Mistilteinn in good condition.</i>

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.700
<i>On course for impact with target.</i>

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.080
<i>Impact in five seconds.</i>

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.650
I hate to admit it, but NIFL 
did better than we did.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.200
We used the horizon and the island as walls,

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.560
and we took the Basilisk's line 
of sight into consideration.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.980
Our plan should've been perfect.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:29.710
How did it detect us?

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.010
Stop.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.950
It didn't use its third eye when it pursued us.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.920
It could've reached us if it had used its third eye.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.340
Shinomiya-sensei.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.340
What is it?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.230
I'd like to talk to Loki Jotunheim of NIFL.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.760
Of NIFL?

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.230
<i>Hey, Lieutenant Mononobe.</i>

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:06.000
<i>I was just about to contact you.</i>

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:10.900
<i>Regarding the girl with 
the color-changed Ryumon.</i>

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.150
I don't intend to kill Tear.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.370
<i>I've heard your operation failed.</i>

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>Are you suggesting that 
you have another plan?</i>

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:22.280
Yes.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:28.540
Could you possibly convince them to 
hand over a Mistilteinn, Major Loki?

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:30.560
<i>A Mistilteinn?</i>

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.260
I doubt it's been mass-produced,

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.920
but there must still be a prototype.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.230
<i>It failed to reach the Basilisk, did it not?</i>

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.850
<i>Why would you want such a thing?</i>

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:46.560
I don't believe the Mistilteinn's 
design is conceptually flawed.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:51.020
If we use it, there's a chance 
we can defeat the Basilisk.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.290
<i>You seem pretty confident.</i>

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.140
<i>I'll do what I can.</i>

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.080
<i>But there won't be a next time.</i>

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.540
<i>Keep that in mind, Lieutenant Mononobe.</i>

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.300
There's something you so 
desperately want to protect, huh?

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.230
That Fafnir...

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.220
It's me.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.320
Connect me to Major General Dylan.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.140
I believe this strategy by NIFL

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.950
was the most effective against the Basilisk.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.570
What the Mistilteinn didn't have

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.870
was an adequate amount of mithril armor.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:44.920
That means,

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:48.670
if we Ds can make up for that 
with matter conversions...

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:52.080
We could use it to defeat 
the Basilisk, is that right?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.600
Yes.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.800
That may be true in theory,

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.760
but the third eye disintegrates 
even mithril in an instant.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.720
Is it not true that NIFL gave up 
because they determined

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.080
that no amount of mithril would suffice?

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.940
That's if it kept firing the Catastrophe.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.900
What do you mean?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.070
The Basilisk, until now,

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.610
has fired the Catastrophe 
twice from its third eye.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.240
It had a discharge time of 
roughly five seconds both times.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:27.650
Additionally, it could have 
fired in quick succession

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:31.360
when it was fighting us, but it didn't.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:35.080
It's natural to assume that 
it's because there's a risk.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:39.830
There's a limit to how much dark matter 
we can produce at any moment.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.100
The same might be true of the Basilisk, too.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.210
I wonder if it discharges everything it has.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:50.740
It was definitely overkill for the Mistilteinn.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.560
Maybe it gets emptied in five seconds.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:58.540
So it's defenseless right after it attacks?

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:02.280
Maybe we can defeat it really 
easily at that moment.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.620
That would make things easy.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.400
We should assume

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:11.250
it'll continue attacking as 
usual with its other two eyes.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.500
Then what do we do?

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:16.850
That's where we use the Mistilteinn.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:21.940
It's designed to be able to withstand 
the main Catastrophe attack.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:22.960
I get it!

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.680
So with enough added mithril to 
defend it for five seconds' worth

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.180
of an attack from the third eye...

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:31.390
In theory, it would reach the Basilisk.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:33.600
Yeah.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.570
I believe it's worth consideration.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.570
I agree.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.820
Let's come up with a new 
strategy based on this idea.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.360
All right, let's do it.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.350
Yeah.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:48.620
We're just getting started.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.030
Yuu-san.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.820
Can I talk to you?

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:56.570
Sure.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.510
Do you

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:06.320
really believe this strategy will work?

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:10.590
Can we really defeat the Basilisk?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.560
If we fail this time, Tear-san won't...

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:17.320
We have to do what we can.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:20.730
The Basilisk might detect our attack again.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.700
The Mistilteinn can control its descent.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.080
We'll have to work out the details of the plan,

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:29.600
but if we can complement it with the Ds' help...

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.830
Are you against it?

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.470
I think the Basilisk can react so fast

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:43.960
because it has another, different ability.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:45.510
Different?

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:49.970
The Catastrophe blows away time.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:55.150
The Basilisk may be able to see 
what's at the end of that time.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.630
The end of that time?

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:58.940
Mononobe!

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:00.640
Iris.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.290
Come quick, Mononobe.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.400
It's Mitsuki-chan and Lisa-chan!

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:08.370
Yuu...

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.790
I'll ask again.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.330
Do you really mean what you're saying?

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:15.960
Of course.

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:19.090
I'll descend along with the Mistilteinn.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:21.040
Mitsuki...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.800
The warhead will be too large 
in our next operation.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.950
The descent controls won't work.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:32.040
So someone has to descend with the Mistilteinn

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:34.730
to adjust its trajectory.

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:36.450
And I'm asking you

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:40.980
why you should take on such a role yourself!

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.120
As with the previous operation,

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:49.530
the Basilisk's abilities may 
exceed our expectations.

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:53.920
I can't hand over such a 
dangerous task to anyone else.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:54.910
Mitsuki-san!

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:59.470
Please take care of Tear-san 
if worst comes to worst.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.920
If worst comes to worst?

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:08.080
Do you really think that's acceptable?

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.960
Why do you always—

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.200
I don't need your approval.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:18.520
This is my decision as the captain.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.350
Mitsuki-chan...

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:25.820
Wait.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:27.360
Fyril-san.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.570
If someone has to do it,

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:32.910
I will.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:37.160
No. This is something I have to do.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:41.770
No, if we're to consider the worst case scenario,

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.130
then I'm best suited to do it.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:46.160
You're the captain, so you have to remain, Mitsuki.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:49.500
Then it could be me, too, right?

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:50.300
Yeah.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.260
Me, too.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.040
You can't even fly, Iris-san.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:57.890
That's true, but...

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.220
I can't let anyone go by themselves.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:03.120
I also volunteer.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.270
Nii-san!

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:10.450
I know, Mitsuki-san.

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:12.200
I've decided.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:15.870
I've chosen the condition it would 
take for me to forgive you.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:23.580
I demand that you include 
all volunteers, including me,

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:26.750
in a perfect strategy of your devising

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:31.760
that could respond to any 
unforeseen circumstances.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:36.220
And bring everyone back safely.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:37.770
Everyone?

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:40.500
If you can do that,

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:44.270
I'll forgive you.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.830
It's not going so well.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:04.650
I can't believe you'd oppose me, too.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.110
What did you expect?

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:08.830
I'm going with you, even if 
I have to claw my way there.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.300
I'm not leaving you alone.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:05.700
You've always been so...

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.940
Stubborn.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.630
You made that promise to me

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.490
when we were kids, too.

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:23.160
That you'd never leave me alone.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.460
Y-Yeah.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:28.660
<i>When did that happen?</i>

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.170
You have to work hard, too.

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:35.540
You want Lisa to forgive you, don't you?

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.220
Okay.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.640
I'll come up with a new strategy.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.330
Hey!

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:03.780
Hang in there!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.810
Mononobe-san...

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.360
What happened?

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:08.280
Where's Tear?

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:15.830
<i>It couldn't be.</i>

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:26.180
Honoka!

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:28.020
What are you doing?

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.740
So long as this girl is here,

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:38.700
you and the others are the Basilisk's targets.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:45.760
We must minimize the loss of Ds.

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:50.830
I could have taken her anytime I wanted to.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:54.770
But it seems we've reached our limit.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.400
Your plan is at a dead end, too.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:19:59.300
Honoka!

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:01.530
I think Tear would be happier

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.330
becoming a Dragon

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.360
than becoming a corpse.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.470
Bring her back to the sick bay.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:44.940
You...

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.660
I figured the easiest way to find Tear

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:53.510
after she was taken by NIFL would be 
to disguise myself as someone else

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:55.450
and let her be sent to Midgar.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.260
With biological conversion,

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.740
I can change my form as much as I like.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:02.840
Honoka?

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.420
Honoka.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:24.060
I liked this name quite a bit.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:29.390
But I think I'd like you 
to call me by my real name.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.270
Kili!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.140
I'm glad to see you again,

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:01.820
Yuu.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.670
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:40.570 --> 00:23:42.850
Honoka... No, Kili.

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:44.770
You've been deceiving us all along.

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:46.730
I won't let you have Tear.

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:49.500
I won't let her become a Basilisk's mate.

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:51.630
What about you, Kili?

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:54.750
Do you want to live as a Dragon, or...

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:59.750
Next time on <i>Unlimited Fafnir</i>: 
"Unlimited Fafnir."

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:05.900
Iris, Mitsuki, Tear, Lisa, 
Fyril, Ariela, Ren...

00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:09.670
We'll decide our future with our own hands!

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:19.840
<b>Illustration: Pirason</b>
